course: dictionary
lesson: 13079
title: Old-fashioned words and mild swearing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are old-fashioned, and people used them long ago. «Oh, fiddlesticks!» is one of them. Grandad might say it when he drops the teapot. It shows he is annoyed, but he does not use a rude word.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If someone says «Fiddlesticks!» after a spill, they are cross or disappointed, not happy. Ask yourself how the speaker feels, then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it fits.
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. «Fiddlesticks! That's not true.» Here fiddlesticks means nonsense, a silly thing to say. The sentence clues tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Fiddlesticks is an exclamation: you say it to show a feeling.
fact: «Fiddlesticks» is a mild word, used instead of a swear word.
fact: «Fiddlesticks» can mean nonsense, as in «Fiddlesticks! That's not true.»
fact: «Fiddlesticks» can also mean the bow used to play a fiddle, but this meaning is rare.
fact: Old-fashioned words often sound funny today, so cartoon characters and grandparents often use them.
exercise: «Oh, fiddlesticks!» Grandma cried when the cake fell on the floor. What does fiddlesticks show? | Fear of the dark | Tiredness after a run | Delight at a party | *Annoyance
exercise: «Fiddlesticks! That's not true.» What does fiddlesticks mean here? | A kind hello | A fiddle bow | *Nonsense | A loud song
exercise: Which word is a mild, old-fashioned exclamation? | Carpet | Sprinted | *Fiddlesticks | Umbrella
test: «Oh, fiddlesticks, I missed the bus again!» How does the speaker feel? | Sleepy | Curious | *Cross and disappointed | Delighted
test: The old man laughed at the silly story. «Fiddlesticks, you made that up!» Which meaning fits best? | A loud train | A fiddle bow | A kind of cake | *Nonsense
exam: «Fiddlesticks» is best described as which kind of word? | *A mild, old-fashioned exclamation | A type of tree | A large animal | A rude swear word
